--- body ---
## Context
Child of 1830. The works reread at stage 2 before 1840 lack the discipline fields. Method and cost proposed before any spend; USD 2 ceiling without agreement. Candidates: Jev pass with decomposed questions (design of the Jev pilot archive 2026-09-30), or the discipline questions of the 1840 prompt alone.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Method and cost proposed and accepted
- [ ] Discipline fields recorded in the dimensions table for all works concerned, counts reported
- [ ] Validation on the 1840 gold set
- [ ] The catch-up writes the discipline fields without touching the ICF labels: `corpus_icf_stage2.py parse` appends an `icf_screen` row for every answer and the REL view takes the last stage-2 row, so a catch-up parsed as stage 2 would overwrite or shadow the existing ICF labels. Write through a dimensions-only path, or under a distinct stage. No dimensions-only parse mode exists yet (PR 1652 left it out: its answer format depends on the method chosen here)
